# Third-party licences

Project code is Apache-2.0 (see `LICENSE`). This file records every third-party
work that ships **inside** the repository, with provenance, so the audit trail
is a lookup and not an archaeology dig.

Game content (`original/`, `references/`, `captures/`) is never committed, so it
never appears here. Tool builds fetched as infrastructure (`tools/spice86/`,
`tools/reko/`) are gitignored and are not distributed by this repository.

## font8x8 — Public Domain

- **Where:** `engine/src/core/font8x8_basic.h`
- **What:** 8x8 monochrome bitmap font, U+0000..U+007F, used for engine text
  (status band, menu, creation form) in the framebuffer.
- **Author:** Daniel Hepper <daniel@hepper.net>, derived from an earlier header
  by Marcel Sondaar citing "International Business Machines (public domain VGA
  fonts)".
- **Source:** https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8 , file `font8x8_basic.h`,
  fetched 2026-10-20.
- **Licence:** Public Domain (per the file's own header). No attribution is
  required by the licence; it is given here anyway so the provenance is
  auditable. Decision and rejected alternatives (Px437 CC-BY-SA, romfont
  unlicensed, SeaBIOS GPL, scriven OFL): `docs/phase4-kickoff-cp4b.md`
  § "Font licensing decision".
- **Modifications:** the array declaration was changed from
  `char font8x8_basic[128][8]` to `static const unsigned char` so the header
  can be included by one translation unit without external linkage. The glyph
  bytes are untouched.

## Substitute tile art — our own authored work (Apache-2.0)

Recorded here although it is **not** third-party work, because provenance is the
reason this file exists and this is the one asset whose authorship could plausibly
be questioned.

- **Where:** `engine/assets/tiles/cleanroom/tiles/` (64 SVGs) and the generated
  `engine/src/core/tiles_cleanroom.h`.
- **What:** original substitute tile art for the reconstruction. It communicates
  the same things as the game's CGA tiles; it is not a copy of them.
- **Licence:** Apache-2.0, ours. See `LICENSE`.
- **How it was made:** cleanroom procedure. A spec author who had examined the
  original binary wrote intent-only requirements; a separate implementer drew the
  art from the specification alone, in a repository containing no game art.
  Full procedure, verification chain, build history and recorded failures:
  **`docs/cleanroom-procedure.md`**. Legal record travelling with the assets:
  `engine/assets/tiles/cleanroom/PROVENANCE.md`.
- **Specification:** `docs/tile-art-spec.md`. Revision 2 was built against blob
  `46e0d4d8318e0cfd8529892852b5d8f91342a496`.
- **Reproducibility:** `gen/tiles.py` regenerates all 64 SVGs byte-for-byte; the
  header is regenerated by `tools/tiles2h.py` and `make test` fails on drift.
- **A rejected third-party source, recorded because it was considered and
  declined:** the `smithkm/scriven` font (SIL OFL 1.1) was reviewed for the letter
  tiles and rejected *before use* — its Runic design is documented as influenced
  by the Ultima games, which would have compromised the cleanroom. No glyph was
  rendered, imported or traced from it; only its public README and licence text
  were read.
- **Status:** 17 of 64 tiles satisfy their structural rules; 47 remain recorded
  debt in `tools/tile_rules.py` and are printed by `make test`. Parked at no
  priority — see `docs/phase4-state.md` § Backlog.
